{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T15:01:08.877131", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_27d5d136-8563-469e-92bf-fd103c28b57c", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: ¬(A ∧ B) ↔ (¬A ∨ ¬B)\n¬(A ∨ B) ↔ (¬A ∧ ¬B)\n(A → B) ↔ (¬B → ¬A)\n(A → B) ↔ (¬A ∨ B)\n(¬A → B) ↔ (A ∨ ¬B)\n¬(A → B) ↔ (A ∧ ¬B)\n\nWhich of the above is not logically equivalent to the rest? Provide the full statement that doesn't fit.", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "import itertools\n\ndef eval_expr(expr, A, B):\n    # expr as lambda\n    return expr(A, B)\n\n# define expressions\ndef expr1(A,B):\n    return (not (A and B)) == ((not A) or (not B))\ndef expr2(A,B):\n    return (not (A or B)) == ((not A) and (not B))\ndef expr3(A,B):\n    # (A -> B) is (not A) or B\n    return ((not A) or B) == ((not B) <= (not A))  # but need (¬B -> ¬A) = (B or ¬A)\ndef expr3_alt(A,B):\n    return ((not A) or B) == (B or (not A))\ndef expr4(A,B):\n    return ((not A) or B) == ((not A) or B)  # trivial?\ndef expr5(A,B):\n    # (¬A -> B) = (A or B)\n    # RHS: (A ∨ ¬B)\n    return ((A) or B) == (A or (not B))\ndef expr6(A,B):\n    # ¬(A -> B) = ¬((¬A) or B) = A and ¬B\n    return (not ((not A) or B)) == (A and (not B))\n\ndef check(expr):\n    for A,B in itertools.product([False,True],[False,True]):\n        if not expr(A,B):\n            return False\n    return True\n\nfor i,expr in enumerate([expr1,expr2,expr3_alt,expr4,expr5,expr6], start=1):\n    print(i, check(expr))\n", "expected": "(¬A → B) ↔ (A ∨ ¬B)", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash"